---

## Key Sourcing Notes & Data Integrity Observations

**1. GWP basis reconciliation**
The investor deck discloses GWP on two bases — **₹3,982.7 Cr** (without 1/n) and **₹3,475.0 Cr** (with 1/n, statutory). Per the "prefer statutory 1/n basis" instruction, the ₹3,475.0 Cr figure is reported, closely matching the IRDAI NL Revenue Account's implied GWP of ₹3,474.5 Cr (the ~₹0.5 Cr variance is rounding within the Revenue Account statement).

**2. NWP/NEP sourced from statutory NL Revenue Account**
The IRDAI Revenue Account shows Net Premium Written of ₹2,737.9 Cr and Premium Earned (Net) of ₹2,642.0 Cr for YTD Sep-25. These tie directly to the Investor Presentation's KPI table (also presented on a 1/n statutory basis), confirming consistency between both sources.

**3. PAT divergence (IGAAP vs IFRS)**
- IGAAP H1FY26 PAT: **loss of ₹126.71 crore**
- IFRS H1FY26 PAT: **profit of ₹131.72 crore**

This ~₹258 crore divergence is driven primarily by IFRS-17 insurance contract measurement differences (a +₹304.9 crore adjustment per the deck's profit reconciliation table), reflecting differing revenue recognition patterns between the new 1/n premium recognition mandated under IGAAP (effective October 1, 2024) and IFRS-17.

**4. Combined ratio deterioration**
The IGAAP combined ratio rose sharply to **114.1%** in H1FY26 from 103.5% in H1FY25, driven by the claims ratio jumping to 74.3% from 62.5%. The company attributes this to two large corporate accounts written in Q4FY25 with limited corresponding earned premium in H1FY26, due to unearned premium reserve (UPR) treatment under the new 1/n regime — with earnings expected to normalize in Q4FY26.

**5. Net worth cross-check**
The ₹2,955.96 crore figure from the Regulation 52(4) ratios table reconciles closely with the Balance Sheet computation (Share capital + Reserves & Surplus + Fair Value Change Account − Debit balance in P&L account), confirming statutory consistency.

**6. Data vintage**
All figures represent **cumulative period-to-date (6-month)** values for H1FY26 (April 1, 2025 – September 30, 2025), drawn from the Board-approved unaudited/reviewed financial results, the reviewed IFRS interim financials, and the H1FY26 Investor Presentation — all dated November 3, 2025.</ans>
